# Post-Test Cleanup — Phase D: Visual system (PERIPHERY)
#
# ACCEPTANCE CONTRACT (locked before implementation)
# D1.1 GIVEN every reachable assessment input step, WHEN it renders, THEN one
#      large Lucide icon appears top-center above the headline, sourced by the
#      step's explicit entry in one constants map; explainer steps do not render
#      a second hero icon.
# D1.2 GIVEN every FlowEngine `.decision` step, WHEN it renders, THEN the same
#      one-icon treatment appears above its question, sourced by workflow + step
#      ID from that constants map.
# D1.3 GIVEN the assessment crosses a locked chapter boundary, THEN the tracker
#      label changes among "Your move", "Your homes", "Your people", and
#      "Your accounts", and only the question icon/tracker use that chapter's
#      subtle accent while the screen remains predominantly white.
# D1.4 GIVEN a chapter is active, THEN its tracker states chapter position
#      (current of total), retains forward goal-gradient fill behavior, and does
#      not restore the replaced app-wide flat step bar.
# D1.5 GIVEN an assessment option is a concrete noun, THEN its tile uses the
#      centrally mapped Lucide icon; abstract yes/no, flexibility, date, and
#      quantity choices render without option icons.
# D1.6 GIVEN a full reachable assessment run on the target simulator, THEN every
#      question is visually evidenced with no scrolling required to answer, and
#      each of the four chapter boundaries is evidenced by screenshots.
#
